---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import framesRawImg from '../../assets/images/frames_raw.png';
---
<PageLayout title="Frames — Alex Sheen">
  <div class="base_padding">
    <div class="w3-row base_container_padding">
      <div class="w3-twothird base_container_padding">
        <div class="proj" style="width:100%">
          <div class="projtitle white_text" style="width:100%">
            Frames
            <div class="projtext" style="width:100%">
              <br />
              <div class="vl">
                OpenEndedGroup Field2 / AR<br />
                2021<br />
              </div>
              <br />
              For this project, <span class="beige_text">partnered with an MFA graduate student to translate their physical sculptures into an interactive Augmented Reality experience</span>.
              Their work frequently features hinged frames of differing dimensions and explores how their movement can reveal
              new interactions between the sculpture and the space it occupies. Our AR piece extends this notion with the common idea in
              AR of <span class="beige_text">"a world inside a world"</span>.
              <br /><br />
              I used OpenEndedGroup's Field to place virtual objects in the viewer's live camera feed of the real-world environment, allowing the viewer to
              physically walk around and through the virtual sculpture. <span class="beige_text">Our piece utilizes the <a href="https://learnopengl.com/Advanced-OpenGL/Stencil-testing">OpenGL Stencil Buffer</a> to
              only draw the light gray sculptures when they are viewed <i>through</i> a black frame</span>. Each frame is paired with a
              single gray object, but overlapping frames will reveal all of their respective objects. By utilizing the Stencil
              Buffer in this way, we create a metaphysical world within the frames in this AR space.
              <br /><br />
              A non-AR test is shown below. You can see how the red and green cubes only appear when viewed through certain frames.
              <br /><br />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="w3-third base_container_padding">
        <div class="proj" style="width:100%">
          <video style="width:100%" muted autoplay loop playsinline>
            <source src="/assets/videos/ar_final_compressed3.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            Your browser does not support the video tag.
          </video>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="w3-row">
      <div class="w3-half base_container_padding">
        <Image src={framesRawImg} style="width:100%" alt="Frames raw" />
      </div>
      <div class="w3-half base_container_padding">
        <video style="width:100%" muted autoplay loop playsinline>
          <source src="/assets/videos/frames_test_compressed.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
